    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d368">

                <pb facs="0386" n="1064" sameAs="frus:frus1863p2/pg1064"/>

                <head>Mr. Seward to Mr.
                        Pruyn</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 32.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <hi
                                rendition="#italic">Washington</hi>,</placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1863-01-20"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >January</hi> 20, 1863.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> Your despatch of November 20 has been
                    received. The President is gratified with your success in effecting an
                    arrangement with the Japanese government for the reciprocation of national,
                    military, and naval courtesies, and the satisfaction is heightened by the
                    circumstance that the arrangement has been extended to and embraced by the
                    representatives of the other treaty powers residing in Japan.</p>
                <p>The Secretary of the Navy has been informed of the arrangement, and also of your
                    desire that the Wyoming may be ordered to return to Japan in the spring.</p>
                <p>I am, sir, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>WILLIAM H. SEWARD.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Robert H. Pruyn</hi>, Esq., <hi
                            rendition="#italic">&amp;c., &amp;c., Yedo.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
